        "title": "Natural Dye Sources: Plants, Insects, Lichens, Tannins",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Natural dyes come from three kingdoms: plants (leaves, roots, bark, berries), animals (scale insects, shellfish), and fungi/lichens. The chemical taxonomy matters: the same dye class (e.g., indigoid) appears in unrelated organisms. What the dyer cares about is not botanical taxonomy but dye chemistry: which compounds produce which colors, with which mordants, with what fastness."
